BREAK IT — credits and provenance

This project is built on the trust-rail discipline of its estate: a mutation + fuzz
gate ("witness") that proves a test suite actually tests what it names, and a
re-runnable receipt (proof-of-play) that a third party regenerates byte-for-byte
rather than taking on trust. The Sentinel behaviour layer here follows that lineage.

The GEP ladder used by the Sentinel behaviour guard (ALLOW / THROTTLE / STEP-UP /
BLOCK / ISOLATE) is from the work of:
  Gary W. Floyd — Lumiea Systems Research Division, ThunderStruck Service, LLC,
  "GEP-Based Security: Behavioral Entropy Signatures for Cybersecurity and DevOps" (2025).
That work is published as Open Defensive Prior Art under Creative Commons. The GEP framing is credited to it; it is not reproduced here beyond the ladder
concept, and no estate-private material is inserted into it.

Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin, used with his permission.
The compression and codec lineage the estate builds on (κ / the Konomi codec and the
LIGHT template work) is the work of Thomas Frumkin (Konomi). BREAK IT does not ship a
codec; the credit is recorded because this build descends from that body of work.

The Liveware Pilot's feed (feeds/credit-default.csv) is the UCI Machine Learning Repository's
"Default of Credit Card Clients" dataset, DOI 10.24432/C55S3H, CC BY 4.0: I.-C. Yeh and C.-H. Lien,
"The comparisons of data mining techniques for the predictive accuracy of probability of default of
credit card clients", Expert Systems with Applications 36(2) (2009). Only ID and PAY_AMT1..6 are read.

